Your project uses **MSTest v3 (3.8.0)** on net8.0. Here are the breaking changes that **directly affect your code**:

### 1. `[ExpectedException]` removed (lines 9, 16)
This attribute is gone in v4. Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>()`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

Same pattern applies to `Process_InvalidState_ThrowsInvalidOperation`.

### Other breaking changes to be aware of (not in your current code, but worth knowing):

| Change | Fix |
|--------|-----|
| `Assert.ThrowsException` removed | Use `Assert.ThrowsExactly` |
| `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed | Just use `[ClassCleanup]` |
| `TestContext.Properties.Contains()` | Use `.ContainsKey()` |
| `[TestMethod("name")]` constructor changed | Use `DisplayName = "name"` |
| `TestTimeout.Infinite` removed | Use `int.MaxValue` |
| Custom `TestMethodAttribute.Execute` | Override `ExecuteAsync` instead |

### Behavioral changes (no build errors, but runtime impact):
- **`TreatDiscoveryWarningsAsErrors`** now defaults to `true`
